Package: maemo-audio
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends}, pipewire-audio, alsa-ucm-conf, libspa-0.2-bluetooth
Description: Maemo Leste audio init scripts and configuration

Package: maemo-audio-droid4
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 maemo-audio
Description: Maemo Leste audio configuration - Motorola Droid 4
 Volume tuning ladders for the cpcap codec as wired on the Motorola
 Droid 4, published as wireplumber node properties for
 maemo-statusmenu-volume.
 .
 There is one maemo-audio-<device> package per device and exactly one
 should be installed, pulled in by the device image metapackage the
 same way that metapackage already selects leste-config-<device>. The
 image is device-specific even though the initial package install runs
 in a container, so the metapackage choice is the device selection and
 no runtime detection is needed.
 .
 Device packages must be mutually exclusive. When adding a new
 maemo-audio-<device> package, add it to the Conflicts list of every
 existing device package and the others to its own, so two ladders can
 never be active at once.

